(
 '# Server'
 ''
 'The README fetch does not validate GitHub''s certificate.'
 ''
 'Rumba''s <Core.NewClient> sets TLSFlag←32, which means "do not validate certs", and'
 '<Server.FetchReadme> leaves it at that. The Markdown fetched this way is rendered into'
 'our own pages, so a man in the middle could put content there; the sanitising step is a'
 'mitigation but not an answer. Switching validation on needs a CA store configured in'
 'Conga, which is why it was not simply changed. Settle this before the README feature'
 'ships. See "Misc/tatin-readme-implementation-plan.md".'
 ''
 '# Static files'
 ''
 'Files returned by the Tatin server may carry an X-Robots-Tag in the HTTP header with an'
 'appropriate value. We need to check whether Apache returns static pages as well.'
 '(At least the maintenance page is I believe)'
)
